<title>PANAMA: US-Mexican firm to build $150 mln resort in Panama.</title>
<headline>US-Mexican firm to build $150 mln resort in Panama.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S.-Mexican consortium won a 40-year concession to build and operate a $150 million resort complex on a Panamanian military base once used by henchmen of former strongman Manuel Antonio Noriega, the government said.</p>
<p>International Realty Group Inc and Clusters SA de CV of Mexico were awarded a preliminary contract to build three hotels, golf courses and nature walks on the former base in Farallon, 70 miles (110 km) from Panama City, Tourism Institute spokesman Andres Villa said.</p>
<p>Panama's government is scheduled to approve the contract in 60 days, he said. Construction would start next year.</p>
<p>The base, once used by Noriega's notorious Panama Defense Forces, was turned over to Panamanian control from the United States military in the 1970s.</p>
<p>-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739</p>
